What KAVACH adapted from piolium
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

KAVACH keeps its own original core (the six operator-nightmare kill chains and
attack-trees, the VAPT verdict + fail-closed certification gate, CVSS severity
chaining, the zero-input recon, the Docker-first scanner suite, and the VAJRA
persona). The following designs are adapted from piolium and re-implemented for
KAVACH's Claude Code skill + Python architecture:

  - The multi-mode audit model and per-mode phase decomposition (KAVACH ships
    lite / balanced / deep / diff / confirm / revisit / merge / longshot),
    re-expressed with KAVACH phase ids.
  - The resumable, gate-driven run-state design (audit-state.json schema, phase
    status lifecycle, prerequisite DAG, retry/backoff bookkeeping, resume
    selection) - re-implemented in Python.
  - The controlled-concurrency scheduler and phase-runner design.
  - The structured output layout: the durable attack-surface knowledge base, the
    findings-draft -> findings/<id>-<slug>/ promotion tree (draft.md, report.md,
    poc, evidence/), and the consolidated final report - re-skinned to KAVACH's
    .kavach/ artifact tree.
  - The review-chamber, deep-probe, false-positive-verification, variant-search,
    PoC-construction, and confirmation pipelines, ported as KAVACH sub-agents
    (agents/kavach-*.md).
  - The per-finding disclosure-report contract and false-positive-elimination
    gates.
  - Companion analysis skills (skills/): CodeQL, CI/AI-agent-actions auditing,
    threat modeling, spec-to-code compliance, variant analysis, zeroize/secret
    -wipe auditing, and Semgrep rule authoring.

Files that were ported near-verbatim carry an inline provenance note. See
individual agents/kavach-*.md, skills/*/SKILL.md, and skill/references/*.md
headers.
